  "id": "between-subjects-analysis-of-variance",
  "term": "between-subjects analysis of variance",
  "definition": "Between-subjects analysis of variance is a statistical method used to test whether outcome scores differ across separate groups of participants. In this study, a two-way between-subjects ANOVA compared scores by study programme, study year, and whether the effect of one depended on the other.",
